# Grand Abolisher: "During your turn, your opponents can't cast spells or activate abilities of artifacts, creatures, or
# enchantments." Bot1 casts it on turn 1. On Bot1's turn 3 Bot2, holding an untapped Mox Ruby (an artifact: its mana ability is
# barred too, this text has no mana-ability exception) and an untapped Mountain, can cast neither Lightning Bolt (the refusal) nor
# tap the Mox for mana. The Mountain is a land, no artifact, creature or enchantment, so its mana ability still works, and
# Footfall Crater's cycling from the hand is no ability of an artifact, creature or enchantment permanent (CR 602.5): Bot2 cycles it
# with the Mountain's mana. On Bot2's own turn 4 the Mox taps and the Bolt is cast.

[Bot1 Deck]
Plains
Mox Pearl
Grand Abolisher
Plains x13

[Bot2 Deck]
Mountain
Mox Ruby
Lightning Bolt
Footfall Crater
Mountain x12

